{"id":"NCT01689584","title":"COsegregation of VARiants in Panel of Genes","official":"Study of Family COsegregation of Nucleotide VARiants in the Panel of Genes to Validate Their Use in Genetic Counseling","summary":"The aim of the COVAR project is to achieve reliable classification of as many variants of interest as possible from the French OncoGenetics Database (FrOG, https://frog-db.fr/) in order to use them for the genetic counseling. The results obtained through this study will have a major impact on clinical management of the patients and their families conducting in some cases to propose a prophylactic surgery.","conditions":["Gene Mutation-Related Cancer","Genetic Predisposition"],"interventions":[{"type":"GENETIC","name":"salivary kit"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\nIndex cases:\n\n* A person carrying a variant of interest in a gene analyzed in a diagnostic setting by one of the laboratories within the Genetics and Cancer Group (GGC)-Unicancer network, classified as class 3, 4 or hypomorphic class 5, and selected by the national expert group for the gene concerned.\n* Age ≥ 18 years.\n* Signed written inform consent \"index case\"\n\nRelated parties:\n\n* Any relative of an index case with cancer\n* Any relative without cancer related to an index case, selected by the investigators, according to family structure and degree of related compared to the index case\n* For class 4 and hypomorphic class 5 variants; relatives currently undergoing analysis or having already obtained a test result for the variant of interest as part of clinical care.\n* Age ≥ 18 years\n* Information and signature of the informed consent \"selected relatives\"\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Minors\n* Persons deprived of liberty or under guardianship (including curators).\n* Absence of signed written inform consent","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"DIAGNOSTIC","enrollment":11000,"start":"2012-07-02","pcd":"2037-07-02","upd":"2026-09-01","sponsor":"Institut Curie","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Sandrine CAPUTO, PhD · 33172389367 · sandrine.caputo@curie.fr","Isabelle TURBIEZ, Project Manager · 33147111659 · isabelle.turbiez@curie.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"Centre Hospitalier de Bastia","city":"Bastia","pr":"","zip":"20604","s":"NYR","lat":42.7022,"lon":9.4512,"c":"Franck LE DUFF, MD"},{"f":"Institut Curie - Saint-Cloud site","city":"Saint-Cloud","pr":"","zip":"92210","s":"R","lat":48.846,"lon":2.2029,"c":"Emmanuelle FOURME, PhD · emmanuelle.fourme@curie.fr"},{"f":"CHU Amiens - Hôpital Nord","city":"Amiens","pr":"","zip":"80054","s":"R","lat":49.9,"lon":2.3,"c":"Gilles MORIN, MD"},{"f":"ICO - Centre Paul Papin","city":"Angers","pr":"","zip":"49933","s":"R","lat":47.4716,"lon":-0.552,"c":"Marie COUDERT, MD"},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier d'Angoulème","city":"Angoulême","pr":"","zip":"16959","s":"R","lat":45.65,"lon":0.1535,"c":"Stéphanie CHIEZE-VALERO, MD"},{"f":"Institut Sainte-Catherine","city":"Avignon","pr":"","zip":"84918","s":"R","lat":43.9483,"lon":4.8089,"c":"Hélène DREYFUS, MD"},{"f":"CHU Besançon","city":"Besançon","pr":"","zip":"25030","s":"R","lat":47.2488,"lon":6.0182,"c":"Marie-Agnès COLLONGE-RAME, MD"},{"f":"Groupe Hospitalier Pellegrin","city":"Bordeaux","pr":"","zip":"33076","s":"R","lat":44.8412,"lon":-0.5805,"c":"Julie TINAT, MD"},{"f":"Institut Bergonié","city":"Bordeaux","pr":"","zip":"33076","s":"R","lat":44.8412,"lon":-0.5805,"c":"Virginie BUBIEN, MD"},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier Jacques Coeur","city":"Bourges","pr":"","zip":"18020","s":"R","lat":47.0833,"lon":2.4,"c":"Isabelle MORTEMOUSQUE, MD"},{"f":"CHU Morvan de Brest","city":"Brest","pr":"","zip":"29200","s":"R","lat":48.3903,"lon":-4.4863,"c":"Marc PLANES, MD"},{"f":"Centre François Baclesse","city":"Caen","pr":"","zip":"14076","s":"R","lat":49.1859,"lon":-0.3591,"c":"Pascaline BERTHET, MD"},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier Hôtel Dieu","city":"Chambéry","pr":"","zip":"73011","s":"R","lat":45.5663,"lon":5.9208,"c":"Sandra FE